RB-1: dice-entry-dialog.tsx's scrollDown keeps its own function, and its doc comment now says why.
It is an imperative scroll of a DOM node from an event or effect-event handler.
react-hooks/immutability can't tell that node, found through the `form` ref prop, from a render
value being mutated. Written inline, the rule flags it again, and the react-hooks line disables
are at their budget.

RB-4: roll-tray/use-result.tsx, a component file named like a hook, is now used-result.tsx (git
mv). Its component UseResult is now UsedResult, and the private UseStatus is now UsedStatus. The
one importer, latest-result.tsx, follows. All three are private to the tray, which is new in
commit 16, so no other lane's file and no test changes.

RB-5, in part: commandWords (tray-words.ts) spells out its return,
`{ doing: string; done: string; not: string } | undefined`, in place of
`Parameters<typeof wayWords>[2]`. No named type is added outside a types.ts (CLAUDE.md §3; RA-3
removed one such in this round). Naming WayWords and ToastDraft in src/features/rolling/types.ts
joins the Phase 4 item that moves RollToast and ToastBook there.

Names and comments only: no statement changes, no test file changes. L0 (38 related suites, 2,045
tests) green; L1 on this tree: jest, typegen and tsc, eslint and gates 1-12 all ok; next build ok.

